 SH, Choi EK, Lee SS et al (2007) Polyp measurement reliability, accuracy, and discrepancy: optical colonoscopy versus CT colonography with pig colonic specimens. Radiology 244(1):157&#x02013;164 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17507724</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Slater</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Honeyfield</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Burling</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Halligan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>CT colonography: effect of colonic distension on polyp measurement accuracy and agreement&#x02014;in vitro study</article-title><source>Acad Radiol</source><year>2006</year><volume>13</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>850</fpage><lpage>859</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.acra.2006.03.018</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Taylor S, Slater A, Honeyfield L, Burling D, Halligan S (2006) CT colonography: effect of colonic distension on polyp measurement accuracy and agreement&#x02014;in vitro study. Acad Radiol 13(7):850&#x02013;859 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16777559</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Participants in the Paris workshop</collab></person-group><article-title>he Paris endoscopic classification of superficial neoplastic lesions: esophagus, stomach, and colon: November 30 to December 1, 2002</article-title><source>Gastrointest Endosc</source><year>2003</year><volume>58</volume><issue>6 Suppl</issue><fpage>S3</fpage><lpage>S43</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Participants in the Paris workshop (2003) he Paris endoscopic classification of superficial neoplastic lesions: esophagus, stomach, and colon: November 30 to December 1, 2002. Gastrointest Endosc 58(6 Suppl):S3&#x02013;S43 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14652541</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gopalswamy</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Shenoy</surname><given-names>VN</given-names></name><name><surname>Choudhry</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Is in vivo measurement of size of polyps during colonoscopy accurate?</article-title><source>Gastrointest Endosc</source><year>1997</year><volume>46</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>497</fpage><lpage>502</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0016-5107(97)70003-8</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Gopalswamy N, Shenoy VN, Choudhry U et al (1997) Is in vivo measurement of size of polyps during colonoscopy accurate? Gastrointest Endosc 46(6):497&#x02013;502 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9434215</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>